WEBVTT

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.940
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.180
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.020
Calling everything delicious!

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:43.520
The more I eat, the more powerful I get!

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:46.890
Let’s capture ingredients around the world!

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:51.460
I dream of being an invincible 
Gourmet Fighter!!

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:56.500
Now on to the bottom of the 
sea, or the tops of glaciers!

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.170
Jump! Jump Jump Jump! 
Knock! Knock Knock Knock!

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:01.370
Give thanks!

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:04.580
Let’s eat!

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:10.380
Wow wo!! Spiked Punch! Wow wo!! Multi-fold!

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:15.520
Guts! Gutsy Guts! I can eat any dream!

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.790
Wow wo!! My very own... 
Wow wo!! ...Full Course!

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.960
Guts! Gutsy Guts! Gather them all up!

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:31.040
And put the world on my plate!

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:33.840
Wow wow wow! Eat the mountains!!

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.410
Wow wow wow! Toriko!!

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:39.010
Wow wow wow! Eat the oceans!!

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:43.280
Wow wow wow! Tori, Tori, Tori, Toriko!!

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:50.120
Someone once said...

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:55.390
There is white fruit that looks just like 
ripe mango, and when you heat it up,

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:59.960
it overflows with simmering 
yellow fruit juice...

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:04.540
Soft-boiled Maneggo!

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:09.170
There's an island made out 
of sweet, light biscuits...

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:12.280
Biscuit Isle!

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.510
The world is in the Gourmet Age...

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:21.990
An age in which people quest for 
yet unknown culinary delights!

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:29.460
Toriko and Komatsu set out to visit Melk, 
the world's most charismatic cutler,

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:31.560
to have him create a new knife for Komatsu.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:37.740
The other objective of their 
journey was obtaining information

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.040
on a mysterious ingredient, Melk Stardust.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.610
After evading a menagerie of menacing Beasts,

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:46.380
the two finally reached Melk's workshop.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:50.580
Suddenly, Toriko sensed 
a sharp fighting spirit!

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:55.720
Then the famous cutler, 
Melk, appeared before them!

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:03.800
Tension! Toriko's Knife Versus Melk's Knife!

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.940
I <i>am</i> Melk! Cutler Melk!

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.340
What?!

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:16.710
You're Melk, the best cutler in the world?!

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:21.280
How many years has it been 
since I've seen people...?

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:23.610
And what's more,

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:29.790
this is the first time I've ever seen 
anyone so intensely astonished...

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:35.660
I never imagined you would be such a slim,

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:38.060
ridiculously handsome young man, Melk-san...

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.870
I was sure you would be like this...

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:42.770
What kind of image is that?!

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:45.140
Well, from all the rumors floating around...

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:48.140
I was pretty sure he'd be this kind of guy...

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:50.170
I can't even imagine such a character.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:55.910
But the rumors going around about 
me aren't necessarily wrong...

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:02.590
I haven't had customers in a while.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.060
You're welcome here.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:11.030
Thank you! Yay!

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:19.440
Is this your workshop, Melk-san?!

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:28.680
Knives waiting to be sharpened but 
still sparkling like diamonds...

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.450
And all kinds of incredibly 
rare natural materials...

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:36.750
To a chef like me, this 
place is an amusement park!

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:40.960
I wonder how Melk-san sharpens knives here...

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:47.900
What are these cuts?

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:50.540
A Thousand Specialty Knife!

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.900
It goes way beyond the usual 
all-purpose kitchen knife

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.840
that can cut meat, fish, and vegetables...

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:59.380
This all-rounder can easily cut 
thousands of kinds of ingredients!

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:04.650
It's Melk-san's masterpiece 
and costs five million yen.

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:08.490
So this is a pre-sharpened 
Thousand Specialty Knife...

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:13.460
I wonder just how sharp it'll 
be once it's completed...

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:19.900
Don't touch it!

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.270
I'm sorry!

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.240
Komatsu, look out!

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:49.060
It cut through the stone floor!

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:51.100
That's incredibly sharp!

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:56.800
Were those cuts made by knives?

00:05:57.970 --> 00:05:59.740
Melk knives...

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:03.040
Some of them boast a sharpness so dangerous

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:05.510
that they require a license to wield.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:09.980
I often hear of unskilled amateurs getting 
seriously wounded by using them...

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:18.090
...but I didn't realize they were 
this sharp even before sharpening!

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:20.860
I don't recommend touching that.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.530
The raw material for that 
Thousand Specialty Knife

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:25.130
is a tooth from a Warner Shark.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:31.770
Warner Shark (Fish Beast) Capture Level 55

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:27.930
They're known for matchless 
strength and sharpness.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:29.970
It's dangerous to handle 
that without great care.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:31.970
Warner Shark, you say?

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:34.640
That shark's Capture Level 55...

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:39.110
In other words, you rely on others 
to supply you with the raw materials?

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.210
No.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:43.950
I don't entrust anyone to do anything.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:49.620
I procure all the materials for 
the knives and grindstones myself.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:51.820
Watch your mouth.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:55.860
Melk... There's no way you 
could take down a Warner Shark.

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:58.930
I just don't think you've got what it takes.

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:01.200
W-Wait a second...

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.600
How would you know, without 
finding out for yourself?

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:22.720
Maybe I will find out for myself...

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:24.890
Just kidding.

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:27.760
H-Hold on there!

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:31.030
Sorry for talking nonsense.

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:34.400
I don't care where you 
get your raw materials.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.500
Our purpose in coming here is...

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:37.540
Outside.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:41.170
We're going outside. Now.

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:42.740
Melk-san?!

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:49.780
If you want to know what I'm 
capable of, test me out.

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:52.680
Hey, let's apologize!

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:54.290
Quiet, Komatsu.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.390
You'll help me test something, too.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:08:00.790
The sharpness of this new knife...

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:04.930
Are the rumors right about 
Melk-san's cold-blooded side,

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:08.030
that he tests blades by cutting up Beasts?!

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:12.600
I'm going to fight... together 
with my beautiful blade.

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:15.940
Okay. Fine with me.

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.640
I'll fight you.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:21.550
I don't know why you're this offended,

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:24.880
but it seems to be about 
something important to you.

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:27.450
Something you have to 
stand your ground about...

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.220
Something you need to protect...

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:36.460
Whatever it is, it's something serious 
enough for you to go toe to toe over.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:46.300
Well, not exactly toe to toe. Knife...

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:47.410
...to "Knife"!

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:54.710
What's this?!

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:57.050
His hand blade is chipping my knife?!

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:00.620
Grindstone boots!

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:07.530
Just one scrape and the chipped 
knife is back to normal!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.260
Take this! Scale Shave!

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:13.230
Bring it on!

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:21.910
That was mighty sharp.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:25.480
Who the devil are you?!

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:27.450
Toriko-san!

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:28.250
Toriko?!

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.380
How could you do that to Melk-san?!

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:34.250
We didn't come here to fight, did we?!

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:36.490
What choice did I have?! 
You see, this isn't...

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:37.820
You say this is Toriko?

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:40.690
Are you okay, Melk-san?

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:42.690
Toriko, one of the Four Kings...

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:45.560
No wonder he's so strong...

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.830
Yeah. Come to think of it, 
I didn't introduce myself.

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:51.470
But let me ask you the same question...

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:55.570
Who the hell are you?

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:57.740
Where's the real Melk?

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:12.360
Why do you think I'm a fake?

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:18.530
Why? Who leads their customers 
in through the back door?!

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:23.070
That's not the front entrance?!

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:27.170
The sign is over here, huh?

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:28.670
And even the mailbox!

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:30.140
Then...

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:35.180
That's right. This is 
the real front entrance.

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:41.350
Like you said, Toriko-san, we must 
have entered through the back way.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:44.220
You didn't make this, did you?

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:47.130
It's obvious when you look at the size.

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:49.160
The entrance is way bigger 
than it needs to be

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:51.400
for a normal person to go through.

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:56.670
It certainly is a huge entrance, like 
the kind a really big man would use...

00:10:56.670 --> 00:11:01.410
This is my workshop proper. I need a big 
entrance to carry in large materials.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:03.810
Alright, then how do you 
account for these giant steps

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:05.610
leading to the second floor?

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:08.910
They're just as big as the 
ones going up Melk Mountain.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:13.890
Most likely, this is a combined home 
and workshop made by the real Melk.

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:17.420
The genuine Melk is shy in front of 
strangers, so he made an entrance

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:19.690
on the opposite side of 
where you reach the summit.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:25.730
The real Melk must be a giant of 
a man, at least two meters tall.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:29.300
There are too many things 
that don't add up about you.

00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:31.540
Isn't it just the point about size?

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:38.140
In the first place, I've heard that Melk 
is an old friend of old man Ichiryu.

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:40.350
Friends with the IGO President?!

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:45.480
Even I don't know the true 
age of that old fogey.

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:49.820
You're obviously not even 
close to his age range.

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:51.120
Melk-san...

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:56.190
Ichiryu, the IGO President...

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:02.370
My master is a man of few words,

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:04.670
but he counts Ichiryu as 
one of his few friends.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:06.140
Master?!

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:09.670
The person you're referring 
to as the "real Melk"

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:11.510
is the previous master.

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.110
I'm the second generation!

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:17.620
As his successor, I've inherited all of 
the previous generation's techniques.

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:21.020
I'm Cutler Melk the Second!

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:22.590
The Second?!

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:26.620
This comes as a surprise. Who 
knew that Melk had an apprentice?

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:31.960
Like the rumors suggest, he's 
a shy, silent artisan...

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:34.700
...and I'm his sole disciple.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:38.870
So he passed on his secrets to you alone...

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:41.270
...like handed down from father to son!

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:42.870
That's so cool!

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:46.280
You should've just said you were the 
second generation in the first place!

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.410
I suspected you were an impostor!

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:51.520
You were being rude, Toriko-san!

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:55.490
Suddenly picking a fight, calling 
the second generation a fake...

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:58.590
Who are you, companion of Toriko?

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:00.830
Sorry, I should've said earlier!

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:04.500
I, um, I'm the chef at Hotel Gourmet.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:07.400
My name is Komatsu. I-It's 
a pleasure to meet you.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:10.000
Don't be so fawning! You're 
gonna make me sick, Komatsu!

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:11.770
Hotel Gourmet?

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:15.870
You're the Chef Komatsu that 
made the Century Soup?!

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:20.110
You know about me?!

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:23.920
Hotel Gourmet's Century 
Soup is famous these days.

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:28.190
Your name's even known this deep 
in the mountains! That's fantastic!

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:31.790
I'm touched! Melk-san has heard of me!

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:34.890
Incidentally, Komatsu is also my partner.

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:36.590
Toriko-san...

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:39.600
Huh. I've got impressive guests today.

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:44.700
M-Maybe the first Melk-san 
also knows about me...

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.570
I doubt he's ever heard of you.

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:47.470
Oh...

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:51.310
You see, the first Melk has no interest 
at all in what's going on in the world.

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:54.250
And nobody in the world has any inkling

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:57.120
that the current Melk is 
the second generation.

00:13:57.120 --> 00:14:01.450
But what's Melk the First up 
to? Did he retire or something?

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:04.990
Right now, my master...

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:09.090
...is off getting a stone that'll 
be used to make a grindstone.

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:10.830
So he's still active?!

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:14.470
That's incredible. So he made 
you the second generation Melk,

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:17.340
while he continues to go 
out getting materials...

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:22.210
Um, Melk-san... By the by...

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:26.080
Actually, we came here to ask you a favor...

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:27.850
Not just one favor!

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:29.150
An order for a knife?

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:31.350
Right! That's it!

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:32.950
Okay, of course.

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:35.190
But I fulfill the requests 
in the order they come in...

00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:38.060
So let's see, it'll take about three years.

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:39.560
Three years?!

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:42.730
Good for you, Komatsu!

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:46.030
You'll get that knife you 
wanted... three years from now!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.870
Three years, huh?

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:50.670
If you're backed up with orders, 
I guess there's nothing for it...

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:55.670
For now, I'll just have to buy one at 
a department store to replace this.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:01.910
What's this knife?

00:15:01.910 --> 00:15:05.720
It's mine... I accidentally broke it.

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:08.520
It meant a lot to me...

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:09.520
This is...

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:15.960
Hey, Melk. I've also got a favor...

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:17.800
Actually, more like something 
I want to ask you about.

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:22.530
Have you ever heard of Melk Stardust?

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:23.630
What?!

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:25.740
Melk Stardust, you say?!

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:27.740
Melk, do you know about it?!

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:29.740
Melk-san...?

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.410
What about Melk Stardust?

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:35.310
Right now, we're searching for it.

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:37.020
If you have information about it, tell me!

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:42.290
Melk Stardust is a grindstone.

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:47.630
It's a one-of-a-kind grindstone that 
can sharpen any material in the world.

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:49.460
Grindstone?!

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:53.030
Melk Stardust isn't an ingredient?!

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:55.270
Ingredient? Oh...

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:59.300
I have heard that when you 
use it to sharpen materials

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:01.540
with a high degree of hardness, 
gold-colored powder is produced,

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:04.540
and that can be used as a food seasoning...

00:16:05.410 --> 00:16:06.880
Maybe that's what you mean?

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:09.680
Seasoning?!

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:13.580
Apparently, that powder is composed 
of a new type of amino acid.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:16.050
And it contains components with 
a first-rate savory flavor,

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:18.660
the like of which has never 
been tasted before...

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:21.430
Savory flavor that's never 
been tasted before...

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:24.860
My master is the first person 
to have discovered it.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:29.070
That's why that grindstone is 
now called Melk Stardust...

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:32.000
...but actually, I've never seen it myself.

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:35.470
If I had that grindstone here,

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:39.840
I'd be able to sharpen the ultimate 
knife, like never before...

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:41.850
The ultimate knife...

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:52.890
If I find that grindstone, will you 
make Komatsu's knife with it first?

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:53.960
Toriko-san...

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:56.260
Well, Melk?

00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:57.730
It's impossible, Toriko.

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:01.530
Even you wouldn't be able 
to mine Melk Stardust.

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:03.300
Why's that?

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:06.770
It's in an extremely dangerous place.

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:08.740
Oh, I know that...

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:13.540
The old man asked me to get Melk 
Stardust as part of my training.

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:16.810
Naturally, it would be located 
in a really dangerous place.

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:24.390
My master headed off for there 
and still hasn't come back.

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:26.590
The first generation Melk?!

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:29.590
So when you said he was off getting a stone,

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:32.060
you meant he's mining for Melk Stardust?!

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:33.030
Yes...

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:38.540
My master never relied on anyone 
but used his own strength

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:42.640
to do everything himself, from forging 
blades to obtaining materials.

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:45.080
And your master was really the one

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:48.980
who took down a Capture Level 
55 Warner Shark, wasn't he?

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.780
I'm sorry, Toriko.

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:54.590
I knew it wasn't you.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:56.620
As strong as my master is...

00:17:56.620 --> 00:18:01.190
...and even though he originally 
discovered and mined Melk Stardust...

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:03.360
...he hasn't returned in six years!

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:04.430
Six years?!

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:05.530
Maybe he's...

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:07.300
My master is alive!

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:10.300
If he isn't, then I haven't... 
I haven't done anything...

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:11.300
Melk-san...

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:16.840
Tell me. Where can I find Melk Stardust?

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:22.510
If the first generation Melk is 
there, I'll bring him back alive.

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:24.250
That's a promise!

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:25.580
Toriko...

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:26.850
Toriko-san!

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:28.450
Act now and it's your lucky day!

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:30.920
Wait until tomorrow, and luck 
will never come your way!

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:33.120
Then we'll be leaving right away, huh?

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:34.830
First, we have to fortify 
ourselves with a meal!

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:38.160
I'll leave the cooking to you, Komatsu!

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:39.730
Right!

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:41.600
Perfect timing.

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:45.270
Sky Squid (Mammalian Beast) Capture Level 39

00:18:48.570 --> 00:18:52.340
I give thanks for all this world's bounty.

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:54.110
Let's eat!

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.550
Flying Knife!

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:11.060
This is Toriko's capability!

00:19:14.470 --> 00:19:19.740
Chef Komatsu... That knife is wonderful, 
sure, but the way he cuts with it...

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:22.640
He's definitely no run-of-the-mill chef.

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:26.580
Sorry! I didn't realize you were there...

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:30.720
I always bring this knife 
along with me when I travel...

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:31.920
Is there something wrong?

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:34.550
No. Nothing.

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:36.020
Oh...

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:38.660
Come to think of it, it's been years

00:19:38.660 --> 00:19:41.590
since someone besides me 
has stood in this kitchen.

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:43.130
Melk-san...

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:47.430
As I make this, I'll put in my wish

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:49.770
for the first Melk-san 
to return safe and sound!

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:52.640
Thank you, Chef Komatsu.

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:54.610
Thank you for your patience!

00:19:55.440 --> 00:20:00.650
Honeyed teriyaki Sky Squid 
and boiled tail soup!

00:20:01.580 --> 00:20:03.350
Thank you for the food!

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.150
Delicious!

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:10.190
Superb!

00:20:10.190 --> 00:20:14.630
Good! Eat a lot to build up your stamina!

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:19.100
Yes, because Heavy Hole is 
a terribly dangerous place.

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:23.770
Heavy Hole? Is that where 
Melk Stardust is found?

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:24.540
Yes.

00:20:25.270 --> 00:20:28.640
It's about 30 kilometers 
north of Melk Mountain.

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:39.380
Tens of thousands of meters 
below the surface...

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:43.890
The place's unique magnetic field 
and air pressure has a strong effect

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:47.260
on the planet's gravitational force there.

00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:51.330
It's the deepest underground 
cave in the human world.

00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:54.800
That's where Melk Stardust is mined.

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:03.610
Sounds like this will be good training

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:05.780
for the abnormal gravity 
in the Gourmet World.

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:12.750
Damn the old man... He's prepared 
the ultimate training ground!

00:22:15.010 --> 00:22:16.610
Dishing with Tina!

00:22:17.650 --> 00:22:20.450
This is Dishing with Tina, the talk 
show with a heaping helping of fun!

00:22:20.450 --> 00:22:23.520
Our guest today is the IGO Development Chief

00:22:23.520 --> 00:22:26.320
as well as Gourmet Laboratory 
Chief, Mansom-san!

00:22:26.620 --> 00:22:28.630
Did you just say "handsome"?!

00:22:28.630 --> 00:22:29.690
I did not.

00:22:30.290 --> 00:22:32.460
In this segment, we see 
what makes our guests tick!

00:22:32.460 --> 00:22:35.630
This time, Chief Mansom will do a taste test

00:22:35.630 --> 00:22:38.900
with various kinds of his 
favorite beverage, sake!

00:22:38.900 --> 00:22:41.710
Opposing him will be yours truly, Tina!

00:22:41.710 --> 00:22:46.010
Spiked melon juice, Bacchus Apple 
with soda, Infinite Grape Wine...

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:47.810
Why'd you start without me?!

00:22:47.810 --> 00:22:49.410
Are you trying to wreck Dishing with Tina?

00:22:49.410 --> 00:22:50.620
Jeez!

00:22:54.750 --> 00:22:56.690
Hah? The next segment?

00:22:56.690 --> 00:23:00.160
I'm fine... I'm not even one gram drunk...

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:03.590
Did she just say handsome?

00:23:07.090 --> 00:23:10.020
It's a gravitational wasteland that flattens anyone who enters!

00:23:10.220 --> 00:23:13.560
The as the wild beasts close in, a new technique is unleashed!

00:23:13.800 --> 00:23:16.890
Supergravity! Conquer Heavy Hole!

00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:19.010
Look forward to another heaping helping of fun!
